00:46:19.020 --> 00:46:19.540
Here's Jim McGrady.
下面有请吉姆·麦格雷迪。

00:46:20.550 --> 00:46:35.200
It's the mid-90s, and I'm living in a beach bungalow, and I look out the window one day, and I see three large men in black suits and shades standing in front of a Lincoln Town car doing this.
那是95年代中期，我住在平房里，有一天我向窗外望去，看到三个穿着黑色西装、戴着墨镜的高大壮汉站在一辆林肯城市车前面，正做着这个动作。

00:46:38.320 --> 00:47:05.680
and I know right away that they're there to do one of three things beat me up kill me or more likely make me think that they're there to beat me up or kill me so I flashback right away to the week before where I had bumped into in the local diner and and seeing me had reminded him that the day before I had been on the local news insulting him.
我立刻就知道他们来这里只有三种可能：揍我一顿、杀了我，或者更可能是让我以为他们是来揍我一顿或杀了我。所以我立刻回想起前一周发生的事，当时我在当地的一家餐馆偶遇了，他看到我便想起了前一天我在当地新闻上侮辱他的事。

00:47:06.740 --> 00:47:18.480
So he raised his like slicked head from his steak and eggs and he said to me, you should remember that I can have you taken care of.
于是他从牛排和鸡蛋中抬起油光发亮的脑袋对我说，你该记住，我可以找人收拾你。

00:47:20.030 --> 00:47:26.180
And there was something in the way he said taken care of that I knew he didn't mean it tenderly.
他说“收拾你”时的那个语气，让我知道他绝不是在开玩笑。

00:47:28.010 --> 00:48:26.220
so I'm living at the time beautiful place, tree line lanes my neighbors are retirees and railroad workers and immigrants the problem is we're all in court fighting about whether the residents should stay or go we're fighting for our homes the other problem is that I am very poor at risk assessment so it's my name on the op-ed calling greedy and it is my face on tv calling him an aesthetic cretin i was very proud of that phrase um and that's how come three men are standing outside my window and i try to work i go i'm a writer i go back but i'm going back and forth to the window looking out over hours and as I'm doing this I think three things.
所以当时我住在一个美丽的地方，绿树成荫的小巷，我的邻居都是退休人员、铁路工人和移民。问题是我们所有人都在法庭上争论居民是该去还是留，我们在为我们的家园而战。另一个问题是我的风险评估能力非常差，所以社论上写着贪婪的人是我，在电视上称他为审美品味低下的白痴的人也是我——我当时对这个词感到非常自豪——这就是为什么三个男人会站在我的窗外，我试图工作，我是一个作家，我回去了，但我一直在窗前来回走动，向外看好几个小时，当我在这样做的时候，我想了三件事。

00:48:26.600 --> 00:48:26.920
Two things.
两件事。

00:48:27.930 --> 00:48:29.280
I have a simple thought process.
我的思维过程很简单。

00:48:30.300 --> 00:48:33.560
One, being a wise guy is f***ing boring.
第一，当一个恶霸他妈的太无聊了。

00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:41.220
The whole time they're standing there listening to the bird chirp and checking out their man manicures.
他们站在那里听鸟叫、检查自己美甲的整个过程。

00:48:42.300 --> 00:48:59.820
And the other thing I think is about a guy I'd read about named Clarence Jordan, a white man who had founded an interracial farming commune in rural Georgia in 1942. And this got the attention of the local Ku Klux Klan.
我想到的另一件事是一个我读到过的人，名叫克拉伦斯·乔丹，一个白人，他在1942年佐治亚州农村建立了一个跨种族耕作公社。这引起了当地三K党的注意。

00:49:01.220 --> 00:49:08.060
So every now and then at night they would come by, shoot a shotgun, throw a firebomb at the houses.
所以他们每隔一段时间就会在夜里过来，开猎枪，向房子扔燃烧弹。

00:49:08.390 --> 00:49:51.040
So Clarence had a problem, but Clarence was a disciple of non-violence so he did one thing that you do is you try to find some mundane human activity that you share with your enemy and use it to make them see you as a person so one day he's at the local post office and he sees some clan guys and he goes over and he says hey fellas are you married and they go yeah he says children you have children they go sure he says well you know how out when a baby wakes in the night and it's fussing and you just can't get it to go back to sleep and you're up till dawn and they say, oh, yeah, God.
所以克拉伦斯遇到了麻烦，但克拉伦斯是非暴力信徒，所以他做的一件事就是试图找到一些你和你的敌人共同拥有的世俗人类活动，并利用它让他们把你当成一个人来看待。所以有一天他在当地邮局看到几个三K党成员，他走过去说，嘿，伙计们，你们结婚了吗？他们说，结了。他说，有孩子吗？你们有孩子吗？他们说，当然有。他说，嗯，你知道当婴儿在夜里醒来哭闹时，你就是无法让他安静下来，你一直醒到天亮的情况吗？他们说，哦，是的，天哪。

00:49:52.380 --> 00:50:00.860
And he said, well, when you shoot at us, it wakes the babies.
他说，好吧，当你们向我们开枪时，会吵醒婴儿。

00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:05.740
And we have a hard time getting him to go back to sleep.
我们很难让他们重新入睡。

00:50:06.620 --> 00:50:57.160
So I take that thought and I combine it with my complete lack of common sense and instead of calling the cops I go out my front door and I go up to the three guys and I say to the big guy in the middle I say you've been out here for a while now you need the the bathroom and nobody was a muscle and the big guy says now we're good and I think Clarence Jordan what am I now what and I said well are you hungry and the This is a quote.
所以我把这个想法结合了我完全缺乏常识的特点，我没有报警，而是走出前门，走到这三个人面前，对中间那个大块头说，你们在这儿待了一会儿了，需要上厕所吗？没有人动一根肌肉，大块头说，不用，我们挺好的。我想到了克拉伦斯·乔丹，我现在该怎么办？我说，好吧，你们饿吗？这是一个引述。

00:50:57.280 --> 00:50:58.640
This is an exact quote from the big guy.
这是大块头的话原封不动的引述。

00:50:58.740 --> 00:51:05.000
He says, well, to be honest with you, I would not say no to a bowl of lentil soup.
他说，嗯，老实说，我不会拒绝一碗扁豆汤。

00:51:16.140 --> 00:51:17.540
And that's how it starts.
事情就是这样开始的。

00:51:17.800 --> 00:51:21.500
You know, like 20 minutes later, we're four of us around my little kitchen table.
你知道，大概二十分钟后，我们四个人围坐在我狭小的厨房桌子旁。

00:51:22.240 --> 00:51:58.440
and and it turns out they're not even mobsters they're unemployed construction workers they've taken this job from because they're hoping he'll hire them to build the McMansions once he kicks us off the land and raises our houses so it's not the soup is not enough to get them on my side, but it's enough that they tell me is a prick who pays them next to nothing and made them get man manicures because he thought it would make them threatening.
结果他们根本不是什么暴徒，而是失业的建筑工人，他们接这份工作是因为他们希望等他把我们赶出这块土地并推平我们的房子后，能雇佣他们去建豪宅，所以汤虽不足以让他们倒戈向我，但足以让他们告诉我那混蛋是个吝啬鬼，只付给他们微薄的工钱，还让他们去做美甲，因为他觉得这样能显得他们有威胁性。

00:52:04.300 --> 00:52:13.160
The end of the story is we made it, we came up with a system for the the afternoons when it got really tedious for these guys.
故事的结局是，我们达成了共识，为这些家伙感到特别无聊的下午想出了一套办法。

00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:17.220
One of them would take the car to the end of the lane and be the lookout.
其中一个人会把车开到巷子尽头去把风。

00:52:17.500 --> 00:52:20.960
The other two would like hang on my couch, watch my TV, take a nap.
另外两个则会在我的沙发上闲晃、看电视、打盹。

00:52:22.260 --> 00:52:23.460
I was writing a book.
当时我在写书。

00:52:23.580 --> 00:52:24.780
I kind of liked their company.
我其实挺喜欢有他们作伴的。

00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:33.660
And this went on for like four or five days until the **** was satisfied that I'd been terrified enough.
这种情况持续了大约四五天，直到那个混蛋确信我已经吓得够呛了。

00:52:36.200 --> 00:52:41.860
And, you know, I'm not going to exaggerate and say that that me and these guys became friends, because we didn't.
而且，你知道，我不会夸大其词地说我和这些家伙成了朋友，因为我们并没有。

00:52:43.920 --> 00:52:50.380
